# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows converts every file to CRLF, prettier reports
# "Delete ␍" on every line, and `npm run lint` returns tens of thousands of errors
# that are not errors. That noise is worse than no linter: it trains the team to run
# the command, see a wall of red, and stop running it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means git stores LF and checks out LF everywhere. Developers on
# Windows are unaffected — every editor in use handles LF — and diffs stop showing
# whole files as changed when someone saves on a different machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Lockfiles are generated. Collapse them in review so a dependency bump does not
# show as a two-thousand-line diff nobody reads.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
pnpm-lock.yaml    linguist-generated=true -diff
bun.lock          linguist-generated=true -diff
